export anchor BoardGameStyle:
    number: 98
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Board game
    idea: The dashboard laid out as a family board game, with a checkered track round the board, each project racing a pawn along its own lane, dice for the totals and a rule card that explains the statuses.
    base: light
    palette:
        boardCream: #f7f1df, the play area, squares and fields
        table: #e9e4d4, the page around the board
        feltGreen: #2f6b3f, the header, the board frame and sheet labels
        gameInk: #1f1d1a, text, outlines, lips and pips
        pencil: #4a453d, captions and meta lines
        redPiece: #c8452f, the Design lane and week two tiles
        bluePiece: #1f4e9c, the Engineering lane, week one tiles and links
        purplePiece: #7a4fa3, the Research lane
        greenPiece: #2f7a46, the Marketing lane and On track
        yellowPiece: #e0a91a, the primary button, the player's pawn and the focus halo, never text
        stopRed: #a8261b, Behind and overdue
        waitAmber: #86520a, At risk
    type:
        One rounded sans, Nunito, Varela Round, Arial Rounded MT Bold,
        Trebuchet MS, system-ui, sans-serif. Headings are 800 and body 500.
        The greeting is 28 to 40px, dice numbers 56px, card titles 22px,
        lane names 18px, body 15px and labels 12px caps.
    layout:
        A felt green header holds a die logo and the brand, pill nav links
        with the current one cream, a cream search field, the bell, a yellow
        New project pill and the user with a yellow pawn. The page is one big
        board, a green frame with a checkered strip of red, blue, yellow and
        green squares at top and bottom around a cream play area. Inside, a
        Player one kicker, the greeting Good morning, Mara. Your move., and a
        red box for the overdue tasks. The four numbers are white dice tiles
        with corner pips, the overdue die solid red. The main column is The
        race to done, six lanes, each a white card with a coloured number
        badge, name, meta, percent and status, over a track of ten squares
        tinted to the pawn, which stands on its tenth, and a chequered flag
        square at the end. The side column has a dashed yellow Rule card that
        explains each status and Tiles won per day, a chart of stacked
        squares. Below, the Turn log shows six cream cells with coloured
        pawns. Columns stack below 1000px.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 16px inside chips, 24px card padding and 28 to 32px between bands.
    density: Medium. Each project is one lane of ten squares, the side column holds small cards.
    corners: 12px on cards, 18px on dice, 6px on track squares, pill buttons and nav, round pawns.
    borders: 3px ink outlines on cards, dice and buttons, 2px on track squares, a dashed border on the rule card.
    shadows: A chunky 0 4px 0 ink lip under cards, dice and buttons, like moulded plastic.
    icons:
        Solid game shapes with ink outlines. Pawns stand for people, pips sit
        on dice and a chequered flag marks the finish. A play arrow for On
        track, pause bars for At risk and a rewind for Behind and overdue,
        each in an outlined pill with the word.
    focus: A 3px ink outline offset 3px inside a 7px yellow halo. In the header the outline is white.
    tone: Game rules language, such as Your move, Turn log, Miss a turn and Go back.
